### coordinator-api refund/feedback gap closure (164c70120)

Follow-up to 81028f594 closing the two residual holes in the same paths.

- **Refunds cancel the job.** `_mark_refunded` now moves a QUEUED/RUNNING
  job to CANCELED in the same commit as the payment/escrow updates.
  Previously a client could refund mid-flight and the assigned miner's
  later submit_result still passed the assignment/running checks —
  storing a result nobody paid for while the client kept the output.
  The canceled job answers that submission 409.
- **Feedback is anchored to one completed job, once.** FeedbackRequest
  gains job_id (required for non-admin callers); the route verifies the
  job is completed between the caller and the agent, and migration
  c3a91f7e5b02 adds a unique index on (reviewer_id, job_id) so one job
  underwrites exactly one review — repeat attempts get 409. Previously a
  single completed job allowed unlimited ratings, inflating or sinking
  trust_score (which dispatch ranks miners by) at will.

